{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>ויסעו</b> — Twice in the Masorah: here and the other, ויסעו ויהי חתת אלהים (Genesis 35:5). To teach: just as there, the fear of Elohim was upon all their surroundings, so too here. Another interpretation: ויסעו there is at the beginning of the verse; ויסעו here is at the end of the verse. There, because Jacob cleared out idolatry from among them, therefore they journeyed with uplifted hand and the Shekhinah before them. But the tribe of Dan, among whom was idolatry, journeyed to the rear and not to the front, for the cloud expelled them, and Amalek was killing them."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:45.173124554Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}